WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.000
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.130
Vanilla! Over here, hurry!

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:49.880
Right!

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:11.920
Disaster

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.420
It's too bad.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.040
We'd almost gotten the Prototype back.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.130
If that AT hadn't interfered...

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.130
I'd call it good fortune.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.670
We outnumber them two-to-one.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.130
Once we've taken control,
we can take her back anytime.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:31.250
Well, I suppose so...

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.500
That's not all.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.000
While he wants the Prototype back,
Gen. Battentain also has other desires.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.330
Don't you understand?

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:45.210
He wants the secrets of Quent for Gilgamesh.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:48.000
And we've been given
the glorious task of getting them!

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.130
That was close.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.130
Yeah. We'll stay on course.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.710
They think we're Gilgamesh soldiers,
so we can take it easy.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.000
But what about Chirico?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.420
He'll be fine.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.500
He had to go off, but he'll be back.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.380
Uh-oh! The Gilgamesh are coming back!

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:45.130
Damn! Did they figure it out?
I'll shoot some missiles at them!

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.960
What'll firing those things do?
There's lots of those ships!

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.080
Wait! Those are Balarant!

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:51.960
They're what?

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:12.330
Great, they think we're the enemy!

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.170
We have to contact them!

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:18.040
Balarant forces! We are not Gilgamesh!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.540
We're on your side!

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.250
Try to understand!
We just stole one of their ships!

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.790
Col. Rochina! Is Col. Rochina around?

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.290
Col. Rochina!

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.290
So, they weren't just after the Prototype.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:50.250
Looks like they smell the secrets on Quent, too.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.580
I won't let them have this world.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.080
Sir, a report for you!

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.420
They're too much for us.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:03.210
At our current rate of loss,
I don't know how long we can hold out.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.500
Any chance of reinforcements from HQ?

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.960
Almost none.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:10.790
Hi there!

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.130
Is Rochi-poo home?

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.630
Guess who's coming to dinner?

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:15.830
Hi, again.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.670
What are you...?

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:21.000
We caught them in an enemy combat shuttle.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.750
They said they know you.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.710
You've got guts.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.210
We just stole the shuttle to escape.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.170
Where's Chirico?

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.920
Fighting in a stolen enemy AT.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.630
What should we do with these three, sir?

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:35.080
Lock them up.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:39.580
You gotta be kidding! We're Chirico's friends!

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:40.960
You got Fyana back, thanks to him!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:41.790
Come on.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.420
Hands off, buster!

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.830
Be grateful I don't execute you!

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.250
Pops, aren't you gonna say something?

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.330
I'd just be wasting my breath.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.210
Shut up!

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.920
I said hands off! Didn't you hear me?

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.750
Quiet, girl! Walk!

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.540
I may be a girl, but don't treat me like an idiot!

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.670
We're all Chirico's friends, you know!

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.250
Don't push it, Coconna...

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.830
Shut up, you useless wimp!

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.710
Find Chirico and get him back here!

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:07.290
Yes, sir!

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.460
C'mon!

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:17.290
Inside!

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:18.790
C'mon, get in!

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:24.000
Is that any way to treat a lady?

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.670
Rapist! Pervert!

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.580
Isn't "rapist" a little much?

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.420
Huh?

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.540
It's you!

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:37.710
I'm glad you're all right.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.920
Looks like we keep running into each other.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.420
Yeah. Wonder why?

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.210
I'm sorry. It's always because of me.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.290
No, that's not what I meant.

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:50.130
Don't worry about it.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.290
We all like you, too.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.920
Not just Chirico.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.830
Hate to say it, but you are a lot prettier.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.500
Right, Vanilla?

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:04.080
Well, I kinda like my girls a little plain, you know.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.460
Oh, so you think I'm "plain," huh?

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.580
Put a cork in it, both of you!

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:12.420
C'mon, Chirico will be here soon. Don't worry.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:13.290
Chirico?

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.500
I think the outcome's clear.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:08:00.250
Intercepted transmissions say the Prototype
is on the Balarant mothership.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:04.080
But that ship will fall to the Gilgamesh soon.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.500
Most probable.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.540
But this is our only chance to steal her back!

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:11.460
Before the Gilgamesh get too near the mothership!

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:14.960
It's impossible! The Balarant are far from dead!

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:19.000
Even if we avoided the Gilgamesh
and got close to the ship,

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.750
we'd still get caught in a battle with them!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:57.500
Holy...

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.460
Retreat! We'll dig in
on the planet's surface! Retreat!

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.380
Sir! We just lost the main drive!

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:10.170
What?

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:11.540
We can't move!

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:17.540
Sir, we have to get out of this section!

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:20.210
What about Chirico?
You still haven't gotten him?

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:22.250
No, sir! The way the battle's going-

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.130
Sir!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.080
Sir!

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.420
It's him!

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.500
Recover Chirico at once!

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.460
Yes, sir!

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.630
As long as I have Chirico, then someday...

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:10.830
Looks like you're losing.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.790
No matter. As long as you and
the Prototype are safe.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.380
Are you going to use Fyana again?

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:21.380
Yes. She may be the trump card
I need for a cease-fire.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:24.170
Anyway, it's been a long battle.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:26.250
You'd better get some rest.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.880
This block isn't being destroyed yet.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.380
Just relax.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:37.330
Of course, we don't know when
an enemy missile might hit, either.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:29.460
What was that?

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:31.460
What's that light?

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.380
Do the Balarant have a weapon like that?

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.080
No, it came from another direction.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:47.460
What the hell? It took out one of our ships, too!

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:48.540
What's going on?

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.670
Chirico, do you know what that is?

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:53.500
It's Quent's defense system!

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:57.040
Right. And this battle's set it off.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.460
Both sides are being annihilated.
What's going on?

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:26.880
The Quent intelligence!

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:30.580
The 3,000-year-old secret power of Quent!

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.880
You're still making repairs?

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:49.380
Yes, sir. The main booster was hit really badly.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:51.630
Hurry! Unless you want to vanish as well!

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.960
God, neither side even had a chance to run...

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.630
Cut all power.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.790
What? What do you mean, Chirico?

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:03.000
I think it may just save us.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.330
Save us...?

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:10.040
You'd better do it now.

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:13.040
That's all we need to do to survive?

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:15.880
I can't prove it, but it's all we can do.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:17.920
Hurry!

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:21.790
Shut down all power systems on board! Hurry!

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:26.540
Lepard! What the hell's going on?

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:27.920
Lepard, come in!

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:31.880
Gen. Battentain!
Have you seen the telemetry data?

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:34.000
I have! Is it a new Balarant weapon?

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.210
No, it's hitting them, too!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.670
What? Them, too?

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:39.630
I don't believe it, but something's happened.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.170
This ship's in danger, too!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.420
Don't panic!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.540
This has to be one of Quent's secrets.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.080
Quent's mysteries?

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.540
Don't retreat! Move in towards Quent!

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:52.130
But...

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.920
Boosters, full power!
Force our way down to Quent!

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:56.880
Aye, sir!

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:00.080
Engines, ahead full!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:00.750
Aye, aye!

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:32.500
Move it!

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:35.290
Shut up, I know! Don't rush me!

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:36.790
You're in no position to complain!

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:42.130
If Chirico weren't with us,
I'd have killed you long ago!

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:43.830
What're you talking about?

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:47.170
You can make Chirico do
what you want 'cuz you've got us!

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.830
Vanilla, cut engines! Let it fly on inertia.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.750
Huh? What?

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.630
Just do what he says!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.790
All right!

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:11.250
Anyway, the energy's incredible!

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:14.210
The lights keep flying out from the Gomor tower.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:17.500
We overloaded our memory bank with all the data.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.460
It's impossible to measure now. Sir-

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:20.670
Gurran!

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.460
Sir, the light's stopped!

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:25.210
What? Why?

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.630
Unknown, sir.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:31.880
But, if we analyze the data we have,
we may find the reason.

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:34.380
Understood. We'll head for you at once.

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:36.880
All ships on both sides have been destroyed.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.880
With no one to stop you,
you can get back here quickly.

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:42.790
What? Both sides? But what about the Prototype?

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:46.080
Don't worry. We're attempting to
capture a Balarant craft.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.420
I'm sure she's on it.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.250
I don't believe it!

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.540
The 6th and 7th combined fleets
destroyed, instantly!

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:58.330
Some new, powerful weapon they've discovered?

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.580
The Balarant were also destroyed!
Why kill their own people?

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:03.250
The reports could be wrong.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:05.830
No, I think a third power may be involved.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:11.920
Our ship's destroyed, not a shred of hard data,
and these discussions are getting us nowhere!

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:14.210
General! I have a suggestion!

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:17.130
Any trouble on Quent isn't for us to handle alone!

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:19.380
We should convene the Galactic Assembly!

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:24.790
No, there's still one more thing to try.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:25.290
Huh?

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:29.290
What if we had an informal
joint investigation with the Balarant?

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:30.380
Joint investigation?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.630
With the Balarant?

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:43.500
We've escaped the danger zone!

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.630
What about that Balarant vessel?

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:48.630
It's switched from powered
to inertial flight and is underway.

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:53.670
I see. They switched to inertial flight
to escape that light.

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:58.000
That may be the key to the light's true nature!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:58.880
Most certainly.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:02.210
All right, prep for battle!
Full speed towards them!

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:02.880
Aye, sir!

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:07.540
Where the hell are we going?

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:09.580
I'm dropping you off on planet Rapiraqi.

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:12.960
No way! We have to stay with Chirico! Right?

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:17.000
Exactly. Besides, you think you can
tell all of us what to do?

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.960
Come on, Coconna! Let go of him!

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.460
This vessel still has a Balarant
HQ commander onboard.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:25.460
You aren't free.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.000
What was that?

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:28.330
Something's approaching us.

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:32.500
What's wrong?

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:33.670
It's following us.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:37.460
Are there any surviving Gilgamesh ships?

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:38.880
No.

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:40.540
There's no IFF signal.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:42.580
Hey, try hailing it!

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.710
I dunno if that's such a hot idea...

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:50.580
Uh, testing. Testing! Skies are clear today.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.880
They're hailing us.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.290
Wait. I'll tune it in.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:03.040
I repeat, your ship is now within our firing range.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.500
Heave to and and surrender!

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:10.500
I'd like your country of origin,
ship's name and commander's name.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.080
That isn't necessary.

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:13.920
What?

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:18.000
We know the Prototype's on that vessel.

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:21.130
Follow the course indicated.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:24.040
And don't try to fight us.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.290
We're not afraid of that light from Quent!

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.960
Who the hell are you?

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:31.290
Wait and see.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.290
We're opening the forward portside hatch.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:35.170
Proceed into it immediately!

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.460
What do we do, Admiral?

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.580
We're screwed.
They could nuke this dingy with one shot.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:45.040
They're not Gilgamesh...

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:51.540
What's your opinion, Chirico?

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.880
Same as yours.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:59.130
I see. We'll wait a bit and then see
who we're really dealing with.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.500
You're the commander, aren't you?

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:20.580
Not a bad title, if you aren't a space pirate.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:24.130
I'd say we've both been playing pirate.

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:26.420
In the name of the Balarant, I-

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.000
His Excellency is waiting. This way, please.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.580
Let's visit him.

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:45.290
Sir, I've brought the prisoners.

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:47.920
Good work.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:50.750
Gen... General Killy!

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.040
Ah, Rochina. It's you.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.830
I see. So, you're a Balarant officer now.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:00.830
Seems both of us were drawn
deeply into our investigations.

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:03.830
I was once a Gilgamesh officer as well.

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:05.830
As you say, sir.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:10.630
Proto One. You've burned our hands quite a bit.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:14.040
And you, the man better than even a PS.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:17.000
Just once, I'd like to see that power for myself.

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.460
And who are these three?

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:23.750
They were just along for the ride, apparently.

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:25.630
Ah, nobodies.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:27.540
Lock them up. We'll deal with them later.

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:31.420
For God's sake, we're not zoo monkeys!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:32.710
From one jail to another.

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:34.130
Shut up and come with me!

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:35.170
Great...

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.380
Well, Rochina. Seems your usefulness
has come to an end.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:41.920
You think so, sir?

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:44.790
God has given us His blessing.

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:48.960
You were after the enormous power
hidden inside of Quent.

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:51.000
And now Quent belongs to us.

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:54.540
Rochina, you will be executed.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:57.420
Executed?

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.540
Kill him along with those three
insignificant people.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:01.380
Yes, sir!

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:07.250
Did you think the God of Quent had saved you?

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.290
Set a course for Quent!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:12.130
Aye, sir!

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:29.040
What's wrong?

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:31.250
Propulsion systems have stopped!

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.040
I don't understand.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:37.000
The machines are undamaged,
but they still don't work!

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.210
Check it out! Hurry!

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:42.210
This is the computer room.
All systems have gone nuts.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:43.670
We don't know what's causing it.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:46.130
This is the control room. Helm won't respond.

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:49.040
This is engineering. Engines have shut down.

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:51.460
Find out what's causing it!

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:54.040
Your execution will have to wait, Rochina.

00:21:54.380 --> 00:21:57.500
Meaning I get to live a little while longer.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.500
I can't express my appreciation, sir.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:06.210
What is it? What's happening?

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:09.290
Wiseman!

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:11.330
Wiseman!

00:22:14.130 --> 00:22:15.630
How do you know that name?

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:16.710
You know it, too?

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:20.290
Sir, the ship's changing course.

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:21.290
What?

00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:25.130
It's Wiseman's will.

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:37.080
I'm not sure what it was, but it looks like
something happened to the three of them.

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:37.960
So it would seem...

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:42.920
Wiseman...

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:46.330
The name of Quent's mysterious,
ancient intelligence.

00:22:47.460 --> 00:22:49.830
As we proceeded into the unknown,
towards our destinies,

00:22:49.830 --> 00:22:52.420
I felt as if the fate of everything
now rested with us.

00:22:55.290 --> 00:22:56.710
Next Episode

00:22:57.710 --> 00:22:59.580
From the darkness of space, it came.

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:01.330
An invitation from the master.

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:06.790
Wrapped in the scent of mystery,
the taste of absolute power is sweet.

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:10.630
There, they will find everything
to satisfy their ambitions.

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:15.290
The seduction of godhood
heightens the desires in all.

00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:18.210
Next time, "Successor"

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:21.000
Who will be God's chosen?

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:25.290
Successor

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:25.290
Next Time

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:47.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:50.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:50.540 --> 00:23:56.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:57.420 --> 00:24:00.830
Whenever I'm alone

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:04.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:10.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:14.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:14.130 --> 00:24:17.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:24.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:24.420 --> 00:24:30.380
Brighter than any other light...
